This code reads analog values from two Seeed Studio Grove Moisture Sensors connected to an MCP3008 SPI ADC via the Raspberry Pi's hardware SPI0 bus. It uses the libgpiod API to control the MCP3008 chip-select line and the spidev interface for SPI communication. The program logs timestamped readings to a CSV file named `moisture_log.csv`. It samples every 5 seconds and implements robust error handling, ensuring clean release of all resources on all exit paths.

