This code sets up the Raspberry Pi Zero W to read data from the Silicon Labs Si1172-A30-GMR Optical Heart Rate Sensor using I2C communication via the pigpio library. It logs the data to a CSV file named `biometric_log.csv`, including a Unix timestamp, HR (bpm), SpO2 (%), and an error flag. The program samples once per second and handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) for graceful shutdown. It checks the return value of every pigpio I2C call, distinguishes between transient I2C errors and a completely absent sensor, and logs an error row with the appropriate error flag when a read fails.

Please note that this code reads raw ADC values from the Si1172's FIFO registers as proxy values for HR and SpO2, as the sensor requires a proprietary algorithm to convert raw PPG samples to HR/SpO2. This limitation is documented in the code comments.

