This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up the SPI0 bus, and reads data from the MCP3008 ADC connected to the two microphones. It implements a basic noise-cancellation algorithm by subtracting the two audio streams and applies a gain factor controlled by a command-line argument. The resulting audio data is printed to the terminal in CSV format.

Please note that this code assumes mono audio (single channel) and does not handle stereo audio. For stereo audio, you would need to modify the code to process both channels separately and output them accordingly.

Also, remember to compile the code with the pigpio library:

```bash
gcc -o audio_sample audio_sample.c -lpigpio -lrt -lgpiod
```

And run it with the desired gain factor as an argument:

```bash
./audio_sample <gain_factor>
```

If no argument is provided, it defaults to a gain factor of 1024.

