```

This code sets up the MAX30102 sensor via I2C and initializes it using the pigpio library. It reads the FIFO data register in 6-byte bursts and computes SpO2 using the ratio-of-ratios method and heart rate via peak detection on the IR signal. Any SpO2 reading below 95% or heart rate reading above 100 BPM is logged to `health_log.txt` with ISO 8601 timestamps. The code handles I2C errors, sensor-absent conditions, and initialization failures gracefully, with error messages to stderr and the log file. It also cleans up all resources, including the I2C handle and pigpio, on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

Please note that the actual SpO2 computation and peak detection logic for heart rate are omitted and should be implemented based on the MAX30102 datasheet.

