This code initializes the I2C bus, reads from the ADS1115 ADC, and uses libgpiod to control the relay and read the reed sensor. It takes baseline samples on startup, calculates the trigger threshold, and continuously polls the ADC. When the distance drops below the threshold, it energizes the relay for 3 seconds, checks the reed sensor, and logs the event. On SIGINT/SIGTERM, it de-energizes the relay, releases all libgpiod lines, closes the I2C file descriptor, and exits cleanly.

