This code implements the requested functionality using the pigpio library for GPIO control and the mcp_can library for interfacing with the MCP3008 SPI ADC. It handles SPI errors with up to 3 retries, logs moisture readings and pump activations/deactivations with timestamps, and accepts command-line options for threshold, duration, and sleep interval. The program also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to shut down gracefully, ensuring the pump is turned off on all exit paths.

Please note that you need to install the pigpio and mcp_can libraries before compiling this code. You can install them using the following commands:

```sh
git clone https://github.com/joan29/pigpio.git
cd pigpio
make
sudo make install

git clone https://github.com/joan29/mcp_can.git
cd mcp_can
make
```

To compile the code, use the following command:

```sh
gcc -o irrigation_control irrigation_control.c -lpigpio -lmcp_can
```

Make sure to run the compiled program with elevated privileges (`sudo`) as it requires access to GPIO pins.

