This code implements a basic clap detector using the MAX9814 electret microphone amplifier connected to GPIO26 (MIC_PIN) and an LED on GPIO16 (LED_PIN). The pigpio library is used for bit-banged ADC sampling and GPIO control. The program runs continuously, sampling the ADC every 10 ms, and turns on the LED when the signal exceeds the threshold. A debounce mechanism is applied to avoid false triggers. On receiving a SIGINT (Ctrl+C), the program cleans up and terminates gracefully.

