This code captures a single 1920x1080 JPEG image from a USB camera at `/dev/video0` and saves it to "image.jpg". It uses the V4L2 API with memory-mapped (MMAP) buffers, checks every ioctl, open, mmap, and fopen return value, and releases resources on all exit paths. It also installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler for clean shutdown.

