This code sets up a PIR motion sensor connected to GPIO17 on a Raspberry Pi Zero W, capturing JPEG images using the Raspberry Pi Camera Module v2 when motion is detected. The images are saved with a timestamped filename in the `/home/pi/images` directory. The program uses libgpiod for GPIO input and the libcamera-still utility for image capture. It logs all events with timestamps to `/home/pi/motion_capture.log`. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to cleanly release resources and close file descriptors.

