This code initializes pigpio, sets up the LED on GPIO 18, and opens the I2C bus 1 for communication with the CH201 sensor. It reads the distance from the sensor, retries failed I2C operations, and maps the distance to a blink frequency. The LED blinks at half the calculated frequency for a smooth transition between samples. Timestamped distance and frequency are logged to stdout. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for clean shutdown, closing the I2C handle, turning off the LED, and terminating pigpio.

