This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up signal handling for SIGINT and SIGTERM, and reads data from the SDP32 sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x21. It sends the continuous-measurement command bytes, polls 9 bytes per reading, verifies the CRC-8 checksum, and converts the raw pressure using the provided scale factor. Each timestamped reading is logged to the console at a default sampling interval of 1000 ms, which can be configured via a command-line argument. The program handles I2C communication failures, sensor-absent scenarios, and bus errors, releasing resources on all exit paths.

