This code implements a PID-controlled greenhouse heater using a DS18B20 temperature sensor and a 12V heater controlled by a relay and hardware PWM on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. The setpoint temperature and PID gains are provided as command-line arguments. Every 5 seconds, the average temperature, setpoint, PID output, and PWM duty cycle are logged to greenhouse.log. The code uses libgpiod for all GPIO control and handles errors and resource release on all exit paths.

