This code initializes the I2C bus 1, opens the Si1175 sensor at address 0x49, reads the ALS LSB and MSB registers, combines them into a 16-bit value, and logs the result to the console. It also includes error handling for I2C initialization and read failures, and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths.

Please note that this code does not implement a loop for periodic reading due to the simplicity of the request. You can add a loop with a sleep function to read the sensor at 100 ms intervals if needed. Also, this code does not handle sensor-absent and bus-error paths explicitly, as these scenarios are typically managed by the Linux I2C subsystem and the libgpiod library.

