This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up the specified GPIO pins as outputs, and configures PWM for hardware dimming control. It then enters a loop to simulate a sunrise effect, incrementing the duty cycle every second for 30 minutes. The duty cycle is logged with a timestamp to "smart_lighting.log". On SIGINT or SIGTERM, the program gracefully terminates, releasing resources by setting PWM frequency to zero and changing the GPIO mode to input before terminating the pigpio library.

