This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up a GPIO pin for input, and continuously checks for motion. Upon detecting motion, it records a 5-second video using raspivid and logs the event with an ISO 8601 timestamp. The code implements debouncing to prevent multiple triggers within a 200 ms interval. It also handles errors gracefully and terminates cleanly when a SIGINT (Ctrl+C) is received.

Please ensure that you have the pigpio library installed (`sudo apt-get install pigpio`) and that the video and log directories exist before running the program.

