This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up GPIO pins for the HC-SR04 sensor, configures interrupt callbacks for rising and falling edges on the ECHO pin, and starts a measurement loop that sends a 10 µs trigger pulse every 200 ms. It measures the echo pulse width, discards readings that exceed the maximum range or timeout, and logs valid distance measurements in centimeters with nanosecond-precision timestamps to distance_log.txt. The code handles errors during pigpio initialization, file opening, and sensor timeouts, and uses a mutex to protect shared variables updated from interrupt context. A SIGINT handler cancels callbacks, closes the file, terminates pigpio, and destroys the mutex before exiting.

