This code implements a closed-loop speed control system for two DC motors driven by a DRV8833 H-bridge using the pigpio library on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. The code includes error handling, resource release on exit, and signal handling for clean termination. It also detects encoder stalls and prints warnings when a stall is detected. The PI controller runs at a 100 ms period with anti-windup clamping and PWM duty cycle clamping. The code uses atomic operations for shared encoder counters and compiles cleanly with `-Wall`.

