This code initializes the pigpio library, sets GPIO4 as an output for the touch sensor and GPIO17 as an output for the relay. It continuously polls the touch sensor every 50 ms, toggling the relay on a rising edge. If the touch sensor remains HIGH for more than 10 seconds, the relay is forced OFF and further toggles are ignored. The program handles errors and releases resources on exit. It also installs signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to set a volatile flag, allowing the main loop to exit cleanly.

