This code implements a closed-loop flow control system for an ASCO RedHat 8210 series proportional solenoid valve using the pigpio library on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. The valve is driven via PWM on GPIO 18, with enable/direction control on GPIO 23. The YF-S201 flow sensor on GPIO 24 is sampled every 100 ms, and the proportional controller adjusts the valve PWM duty cycle to maintain the target flow rate. The system logs timestamp_ms, flow_rate, and valve_position to flow_log.csv on every control iteration. The program handles initialization, GPIO setup, ISR registration, file open, and graceful shutdown with resource release upon receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM signals.

