This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up the GPIO pins, and continuously checks the rain sensor every 60 seconds. When rain is detected, it closes the window by setting the appropriate GPIO pins and driving the PWM signal. It logs every rain event and motor action with a timestamp to the system log. On SIGINT or SIGTERM, it stops the motor, releases GPIO resources, and closes the log before exiting.

Please note that you need to implement the `syslog_open` and `syslog_close` functions to handle logging to the specified file. Additionally, you might want to add error handling for reading the log file and parsing its contents.

